**Standard error (SE)** – the standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the sample mean under the null hypothesis  

\[
SE=\frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
   =\frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
   \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
   \approx 0.22
\]

So the standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test (i.e., the standard error of the mean) is **≈ 0.22**.
